text:
- settings.replyLanguage [change] Set "Conversation language".
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":60}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.notifications [change] Set "Notifications". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.notificationSound [change] Set "Notification sound". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.linkPreview [change] Set "Open links in the preview". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.panelDefault [change] Set "Default side panel". One of: terminal, diff, preview, files.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","enum":["terminal","diff","preview","files"]}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.panelSide [change] Set "Side panel edge". One of: left, right.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","enum":["left","right"]}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.closeToTray [change] Set "Close to tray". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.keepAwakeWorking [change] Set "Keep this computer awake while it is used". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.resumeInterrupted [change] Set "Resume interrupted work". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.proxy [sensitive, always a card] Set "Network proxy".
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","maxLength":300}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}

- autopilot.status [read] Read an Autopilot run you started (state, cycle, branch): ompdesk_autopilot status.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"session":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["session"],"additionalProperties":false}
- autopilot.start [change] Start an Autopilot run: ompdesk_autopilot start, with its own confirmation card (commit, push or release) and its folder rules. ship defaults to the user's stored level; device runs it on a paired device (default the device your session runs on).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"folder":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"ship":{"type":"string","enum":["commit","push","release"]}},"additionalProperties":false}
- autopilot.stop [change] End an Autopilot run after the cycle in flight, or with now: true stop it at once (the turn is aborted and the run paused): ompdesk_autopilot stop.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"session":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"now":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["session"],"additionalProperties":false}

- remote.list_tailnet [read] List the computers on the person's tailnet as this one sees them (node id, name, login, whether OMPdesk shares it and lets this computer in, and whether this computer already uses it).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.connect [sensitive, always a card] Connect this computer to another computer of the tailnet that shares OMPdesk (nodeId from remote.list_tailnet), so sessions can run there.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"nodeId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128}},"required":["nodeId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.block [sensitive, card unless the user lets agents manage] Keep a device that uses this computer out for good (deviceId from remote.devices): its Tailscale node is blocked and it is forgotten. Unblock with remote.unblock.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"deviceId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["deviceId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.unblock [sensitive, always a card] Let a blocked device (a computer or a phone) connect again while its Tailscale account is allowed, by its block id or name.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"block":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["block"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.set_allowed_users [sensitive, always a card] Set the Tailscale accounts allowed to use this computer, from other computers and from the phone page alike (logins; this computer's own stays allowed when the list is empty).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"users":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"maxItems":50}},"required":["users"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.devices [read] List this computer's device name, the paired computers it connects to (hosts) and the devices that use it (peers), with ids and online state.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.rename_this_computer [change] Change this computer's device name; every paired computer and device sees it at once.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.rename_host [change] Rename a paired computer this one connects to (deviceId from remote.devices): it changes its own device name. It must be online.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"deviceId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["deviceId","name"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.rename_device [change] Rename a device that uses this computer (deviceId from remote.devices): it is asked to rename itself, so it must be connected.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"deviceId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["deviceId","name"],"additionalProperties":false}

- settings.theme [change] Set "Theme". One of: system, light, github-light, solarized-light, sepia, hc-light, dark, nord, tokyo-night, gruvbox-dark, hc-dark.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","enum":["system","light","github-light","solarized-light","sepia","hc-light","dark","nord","tokyo-night","gruvbox-dark","hc-dark"]}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.followAgentTheme [change] Set "Follow the agent's theme". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}

- accounts.github_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start GitHub sign-in. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.provider_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start sign-in for a model provider. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"providerId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100}},"required":["providerId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- credentials.read [never] Read an API key, token, password, proxy credential or the sign-in state of an account. Refused: Secrets never reach an agent. Use accounts.*_status for who is signed in.
- extensions.mcp_servers [read] List the MCP servers this session's omp knows: connected or not, tool count, whether it needs a sign-in, and why one is off (turned off, found only in another tool's config, …).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.mcp_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start the sign-in of an MCP server that needs one (OAuth: a browser page the person completes). Once it succeeds the server connects in every open session, no restart. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}

- settings.get [read] Read the current value of settings rows (ids as ompdesk_app_list shows after "settings."); all rows when ids is omitted. Secrets are never shown.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"ids":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":100},"maxItems":80}},"additionalProperties":false}
- omp_settings.get [read] Read stock omp settings (the ones omp itself lists, e.g. retry.fallbackChains, retry.fallbackOn, compaction.thresholdTokens): paths = exact paths, query = words from a path, label or description. device reads another computer's omp. Credentials and the approval, security, memory and computer-use settings are never shown.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"maxItems":40},"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A paired computer by name or id as ompdesk_sessions lists it, or \"local\"; omit for the omp of your own session."}},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.github_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start GitHub sign-in. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.provider_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start sign-in for a model provider. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"providerId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100}},"required":["providerId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.install_mcp [sensitive, always a card] Add an MCP server (stdio: it starts a program; http/sse: it reaches a service). The user sees the exact command or url first. No env or headers: secrets are never set by an agent.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80},"transport":{"type":"string","enum":["stdio","http","sse"]},"command":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"args":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":500},"maxItems":30},"url":{"type":"string","minLength":8,"maxLength":1000},"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["user","project"]}},"required":["name","transport"],"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.mcp_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start the sign-in of an MCP server that needs one (OAuth: a browser page the person completes). Once it succeeds the server connects in every open session, no restart. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}

- models.list [read] The model role assignments, then the models of the providers that have a signed-in account (each provider's first 40). provider (id), query (words of provider/id) or all: true list whole catalogs, also of the providers without an account (an aggregator's runs to hundreds). device lists another computer's.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"provider":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"all":{"type":"boolean"},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A paired computer by name or id as ompdesk_sessions lists it, or \"local\"; omit for the omp of your own session."}},"additionalProperties":false}
- models.set [change] Switch this session's model.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"provider":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"modelId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["provider","modelId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- models.set_role [change] Assign a model to a model role (default, slow, smol, plan, task, ...); omit modelId to clear the role. device sets it in another computer's omp.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"role":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":60},"modelId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A paired computer by name or id as ompdesk_sessions lists it, or \"local\"; omit for the omp of your own session."}},"required":["role"],"additionalProperties":false}

- app.quit [sensitive, always a card] Quit OMPdesk (every running turn ends).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- app.undo [change] Undo the last change you made with ompdesk_app, when it had a previous value.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}

- accounts.github_status [read] Whether GitHub CLI is signed in and as which login.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.github_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start GitHub sign-in. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.provider_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start sign-in for a model provider. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"providerId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100}},"required":["providerId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- credentials.read [never] Read an API key, token, password, proxy credential or the sign-in state of an account. Refused: Secrets never reach an agent. Use accounts.*_status for who is signed in.

- sessions.saved [read] Saved sessions on the computer this session runs on (a paired host's own when it runs there): title, folder, last change, path.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["local","global"],"description":"local: this folder's sessions; global (default): all."}},"additionalProperties":false}
- sessions.search [read] Search the text of saved sessions.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["local","global"],"description":"local: this folder's sessions; global (default): all."}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false}
- sessions.rename [change] Rename a saved session.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"sessionPath":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Session file path (.jsonl) from sessions.saved."},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["sessionPath","name"],"additionalProperties":false}
- sessions.delete [sensitive, always a card] Delete a saved session file for good.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"sessionPath":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Session file path (.jsonl) from sessions.saved."}},"required":["sessionPath"],"additionalProperties":false}
- sessions.dump_bundle [change] Save a diagnostic bundle as a zip file and return its path: stock's /dump archive of an open session plus OMPdesk's own diagnostics text. Anonymized by default (message contents redacted); pass anonymized:false only when the person asked for the raw transcript. Writes to path, else the Downloads folder. Needs the session open in a tab; defaults to this session.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"session":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Session file path (.jsonl) of an open session, from sessions.saved. Default: this session. A session the person hid from agents is refused."},"anonymized":{"type":"boolean","description":"Default true: stock's /dump anon. false: /dump all, the raw transcript."},"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Absolute path of the zip to write (.zip is added when missing). Default: the Downloads folder."}},"additionalProperties":false}

- sidebar.projects [read] The projects listed in the sidebar of the computer this session runs on (a paired host's own when it runs there): folder path, name, and whether the folder is gone; for this computer also its pin and its own name. Use the paths with the other sidebar.* actions.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- sidebar.add_project [change] List a folder as a project in the sidebar of the computer this session runs on (the 'Add new project' / open-folder path; a folder removed before comes back). path is absolute. A linked worktree lists its main checkout.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Absolute folder path."}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}
- sidebar.remove_project [change] Remove projects from the sidebar of the computer this session runs on, as the project menu's Delete does without its 'also delete saved sessions' box ticked. No folder and no session is touched; opening the folder again in OMPdesk lists it again. path or paths must be listed by sidebar.projects: any other path is reported and left alone.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"One project folder path."},"paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":4096},"maxItems":50,"description":"Several project folder paths."}},"additionalProperties":false}
- sidebar.pin_project [change] Pin or unpin a project in this computer's sidebar (the project menu's Pin / Unpin; pinned projects stay on top). path must be listed by sidebar.projects.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Project folder path, as sidebar.projects lists it."},"pinned":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["path","pinned"],"additionalProperties":false}
- sidebar.order_projects [change] Set the order of projects in this computer's sidebar (what dragging a project does): paths top first, each listed by sidebar.projects. Pinned projects stay above the rest; projects not named keep their place after these.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":4096},"maxItems":200}},"required":["paths"],"additionalProperties":false}
- sidebar.rename_project [change] Give a project its own name in this computer's sidebar (the project menu's Rename; the folder keeps its name). An empty name clears it. path must be listed by sidebar.projects.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Project folder path, as sidebar.projects lists it."},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":0,"maxLength":120}},"required":["path","name"],"additionalProperties":false}
- sidebar.pin_session [change] Pin or unpin a saved session in this computer's sidebar (the session menu's Pin / Unpin). sessionPath from sessions.saved.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"sessionPath":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"Session file path (.jsonl) from sessions.saved."},"pinned":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["sessionPath","pinned"],"additionalProperties":false}
- sidebar.archive_sessions [change] Archive or restore saved sessions in this computer's sidebar (the session menu's Archive / Restore: they leave the lists until restored; no file is touched). sessionPaths from sessions.saved.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"sessionPaths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":4096},"maxItems":50},"archived":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["sessionPaths","archived"],"additionalProperties":false}

- extensions.install_plugin [sensitive, always a card] Install a plugin from a marketplace the person already added (it runs code in every session).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"marketplace":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"plugin":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["marketplace","plugin"],"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.install_mcp [sensitive, always a card] Add an MCP server (stdio: it starts a program; http/sse: it reaches a service). The user sees the exact command or url first. No env or headers: secrets are never set by an agent.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80},"transport":{"type":"string","enum":["stdio","http","sse"]},"command":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"args":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":500},"maxItems":30},"url":{"type":"string","minLength":8,"maxLength":1000},"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["user","project"]}},"required":["name","transport"],"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.mcp_servers [read] List the MCP servers this session's omp knows: connected or not, tool count, whether it needs a sign-in, and why one is off (turned off, found only in another tool's config, …).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.mcp_sign_in [sensitive, always a card] Start the sign-in of an MCP server that needs one (OAuth: a browser page the person completes). Once it succeeds the server connects in every open session, no restart. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.mcp_use [sensitive, always a card] Use an MCP server that only another tool's user config declares (Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, …; extensions.mcp_servers says 'found in <tool>'): copies that one server's definition into omp's user mcp.json. The tool's other servers, skills and rules stay unused.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}

- mobile_web.status [read] Whether the phone page is on and its state (the link is not shown).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- mobile_web.set_enabled [sensitive, always a card for some arguments] Turn the phone page on or off (it exposes this computer's sessions to the person's tailnet).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"enabled":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["enabled"],"additionalProperties":false}
- mobile_web.rename_device [change] Rename a phone or tablet that uses the phone page, by its current name or id.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["device","name"],"additionalProperties":false}

- memory.purge [sensitive, always a card] Erase the user's memory for good: every page, handoff and recorded session.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- memory.delete_page [sensitive, always a card] Delete one memory page (the Memory page's Restore can bring it back).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"workspace":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"project":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500}},"required":["workspace","project","path"],"additionalProperties":false}
- memory.sweep [sensitive, always a card] Run the memory retention sweep for one project (evicts pages the aging rules let go).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"workspace":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"project":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["workspace","project"],"additionalProperties":false}

- ui.panel [change] Open a side panel view (terminal, diff, preview, files), open a session view as a sheet (jobs = background tasks, plan = the plan document, logs, tree = the session tree, work = the work tree), or close the panel.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"tab":{"type":"string","enum":["terminal","diff","preview","files","jobs","plan","logs","tree","work","close"]}},"required":["tab"],"additionalProperties":false}
- ui.settings_open [change] Open Settings at a section (for the user to look at or to finish a step only they may do).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["general","appearance","keyboard","models","agent","memory","tools","permissions","workspace","schedules","connections","updates","advanced"]},"sub":{"type":"string","maxLength":60}},"required":["section"],"additionalProperties":false}
- ui.open_system_privacy [change] Open a macOS Privacy & Security pane in System Settings (Accessibility, Screen Recording, ...). It only opens the pane: the person toggles the switch, you cannot. macOS only.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"pane":{"type":"string","enum":["accessibility","screen_recording","input_monitoring","automation","full_disk_access","files_and_folders","microphone","camera"]}},"required":["pane"],"additionalProperties":false}

- omp_settings.get [read] Read stock omp settings (the ones omp itself lists, e.g. retry.fallbackChains, retry.fallbackOn, compaction.thresholdTokens): paths = exact paths, query = words from a path, label or description. device reads another computer's omp. Credentials and the approval, security, memory and computer-use settings are never shown.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"maxItems":40},"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A paired computer by name or id as ompdesk_sessions lists it, or \"local\"; omit for the omp of your own session."}},"additionalProperties":false}
- omp_settings.set [change] Write one stock omp setting by its exact path (find it with omp_settings.get query). value must fit the setting's type (true/false, number, one of its options, a list, or an object for a record such as retry.fallbackChains). device writes another computer's omp. One step back with app.undo. Credentials and the approval, security, memory and computer-use settings are refused.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"value":{"type":"json"},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A paired computer by name or id as ompdesk_sessions lists it, or \"local\"; omit for the omp of your own session."}},"required":["path","value"],"additionalProperties":false}

- settings.replyLanguage [change] Set "Conversation language".
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":60}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.notifications [change] Set "Notifications". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.notificationSound [change] Set "Notification sound". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.linkPreview [change] Set "Open links in the preview". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.panelDefault [change] Set "Default side panel". One of: terminal, diff, preview, files.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","enum":["terminal","diff","preview","files"]}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.panelSide [change] Set "Side panel edge". One of: left, right.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","enum":["left","right"]}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.closeToTray [change] Set "Close to tray". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.keepAwakeWorking [change] Set "Keep this computer awake while it is used". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.resumeInterrupted [change] Set "Resume interrupted work". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.proxy [sensitive] Set "Network proxy".
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","maxLength":300}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}

- agent_power.set [sensitive] Change what agents may do: OMPdesk control tools, full control, managing or approving for other sessions, tool approval mode, memory, engineering mode or computer use. Booleans take on; tools.approvalMode takes mode.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"switch":{"type":"string","enum":["agentControl","agentControlFull","agentControlManage","agentControlApprove","pstack","ecc","aiMemoryTerminal","computer.enabled","tools.approvalMode"]},"on":{"type":"boolean"},"mode":{"type":"string","enum":["yolo","write","always-ask-cached","always-ask"]}},"required":["switch"],"additionalProperties":false}
- cards.answer [never] Answer an [OMPdesk] confirmation card or a tool approval. Refused: A card exists to ask the person. ompdesk_session_answer refuses it too.

- autopilot.status [read] Read an Autopilot run you started (state, cycle, branch): ompdesk_autopilot status.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"session":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["session"],"additionalProperties":false}
- autopilot.start [change] Start an Autopilot run: ompdesk_autopilot start, with its own confirmation card (commit, push or release) and its folder rules. ship defaults to the user's stored level; device runs it on a paired device (default the device your session runs on).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"folder":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"ship":{"type":"string","enum":["commit","push","release"]}},"additionalProperties":false}
- autopilot.stop [change] End an Autopilot run after the cycle in flight, or with now: true stop it at once (the turn is aborted and the run paused): ompdesk_autopilot stop.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"session":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"now":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["session"],"additionalProperties":false}

- remote.list_tailnet [read] List the computers on the person's tailnet as this one sees them (node id, name, login, whether OMPdesk shares it and lets this computer in, and whether this computer already uses it).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.connect [sensitive] Connect this computer to another computer of the tailnet that shares OMPdesk (nodeId from remote.list_tailnet), so sessions can run there.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"nodeId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128}},"required":["nodeId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.block [sensitive] Keep a device that uses this computer out for good (deviceId from remote.devices): its Tailscale node is blocked and it is forgotten. Unblock with remote.unblock.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"deviceId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["deviceId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.unblock [sensitive] Let a blocked device (a computer or a phone) connect again while its Tailscale account is allowed, by its block id or name.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"block":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["block"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.set_allowed_users [sensitive] Set the Tailscale accounts allowed to use this computer, from other computers and from the phone page alike (logins; this computer's own stays allowed when the list is empty).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"users":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"maxItems":50}},"required":["users"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.devices [read] List this computer's device name, the paired computers it connects to (hosts) and the devices that use it (peers), with ids and online state.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.rename_this_computer [change] Change this computer's device name; every paired computer and device sees it at once.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.rename_host [change] Rename a paired computer this one connects to (deviceId from remote.devices): it changes its own device name. It must be online.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"deviceId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["deviceId","name"],"additionalProperties":false}
- remote.rename_device [change] Rename a device that uses this computer (deviceId from remote.devices): it is asked to rename itself, so it must be connected.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"deviceId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64}},"required":["deviceId","name"],"additionalProperties":false}

- settings.theme [change] Set "Theme". One of: system, light, github-light, solarized-light, sepia, hc-light, dark, nord, tokyo-night, gruvbox-dark, hc-dark.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"string","enum":["system","light","github-light","solarized-light","sepia","hc-light","dark","nord","tokyo-night","gruvbox-dark","hc-dark"]}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}
- settings.followAgentTheme [change] Set "Follow the agent's theme". true or false.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false}

- accounts.github_sign_in [sensitive] Start GitHub sign-in. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.provider_sign_in [sensitive] Start sign-in for a model provider. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"providerId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100}},"required":["providerId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- credentials.read [never] Read an API key, token, password, proxy credential or the sign-in state of an account. Refused: Secrets never reach an agent. Use accounts.*_status for who is signed in.
- extensions.mcp_servers [read] List the MCP servers this session's omp knows: connected or not, tool count, whether it needs a sign-in, and why one is off (turned off, found only in another tool's config, …).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.mcp_sign_in [sensitive] Start the sign-in of an MCP server that needs one (OAuth: a browser page the person completes). Once it succeeds the server connects in every open session, no restart. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}

- settings.get [read] Read the current value of settings rows (ids as ompdesk_app_list shows after "settings."); all rows when ids is omitted. Secrets are never shown.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"ids":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":100},"maxItems":80}},"additionalProperties":false}
- omp_settings.get [read] Read stock omp settings (the ones omp itself lists, e.g. retry.fallbackChains, retry.fallbackOn, compaction.thresholdTokens): paths = exact paths, query = words from a path, label or description. device reads another computer's omp. Credentials and the approval, security, memory and computer-use settings are never shown.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":200},"maxItems":40},"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A paired computer by name or id as ompdesk_sessions lists it, or \"local\"; omit for the omp of your own session."}},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.github_sign_in [sensitive] Start GitHub sign-in. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.provider_sign_in [sensitive] Start sign-in for a model provider. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"providerId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100}},"required":["providerId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.install_mcp [sensitive] Add an MCP server (stdio: it starts a program; http/sse: it reaches a service). The user sees the exact command or url first. No env or headers: secrets are never set by an agent.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80},"transport":{"type":"string","enum":["stdio","http","sse"]},"command":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"args":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":500},"maxItems":30},"url":{"type":"string","minLength":8,"maxLength":1000},"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["user","project"]}},"required":["name","transport"],"additionalProperties":false}
- extensions.mcp_sign_in [sensitive] Start the sign-in of an MCP server that needs one (OAuth: a browser page the person completes). Once it succeeds the server connects in every open session, no restart. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false}

- models.list [read] The model role assignments, then the models of the providers that have a signed-in account (each provider's first 40). provider (id), query (words of provider/id) or all: true list whole catalogs, also of the providers without an account (an aggregator's runs to hundreds). device lists another computer's.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"provider":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"all":{"type":"boolean"},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A paired computer by name or id as ompdesk_sessions lists it, or \"local\"; omit for the omp of your own session."}},"additionalProperties":false}
- models.set [change] Switch this session's model.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"provider":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"modelId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"required":["provider","modelId"],"additionalProperties":false}
- models.set_role [change] Assign a model to a model role (default, slow, smol, plan, task, ...); omit modelId to clear the role. device sets it in another computer's omp.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"role":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":60},"modelId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"device":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A paired computer by name or id as ompdesk_sessions lists it, or \"local\"; omit for the omp of your own session."}},"required":["role"],"additionalProperties":false}

- app.quit [sensitive] Quit OMPdesk (every running turn ends).
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- app.undo [change] Undo the last change you made with ompdesk_app, when it had a previous value.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}

- accounts.github_status [read] Whether GitHub CLI is signed in and as which login.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.github_sign_in [sensitive] Start GitHub sign-in. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}
- accounts.provider_sign_in [sensitive] Start sign-in for a model provider. Only starts the existing sign-in flow (a browser page or a code the person completes); it never reads or stores a credential.
  args: {"type":"object","properties":{"providerId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100}},"required":["providerId"],"additionalProperties":false}
